### How it works under the hood  

| Component | Role | Communication |
|-----------|------|---------------|
| **Producer** (`src/worker-producer.ts`) | Generates numbers 1‑5, posts each to a `MessagePort`. The orchestrator receives that port and treats it as an *output channel*. Once finished it closes the port. |
| **Transformer** (`src/worker-transformer.ts`) | Reads from its input port (the same channel), converts each number → word, posts result back on the same port. Because we reuse the same `MessagePort`, downstream stages see exactly the transformed payload. |
| **Consumer** (`src/worker-consumer.ts`) | Listens for messages on its own port and prints them prefixed with `*`. The orchestrator never waits; it just awaits both ports to finish before exiting. |

